#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The interface lab: Sane UI's Lua drawn in the browser as the game would draw it (Doc/guides/ui-lab.md).

  dev/tools/ui-lab serve [--port 8774]     the lab in a browser, on 127.0.0.1 port 8774
  dev/tools/ui-lab check [SCENE]           runs a scene headless for a few seconds, prints its log; exit 1 on errors

The page runs the code of a scene (dev/uilab/scenes/) under Lua 5.1 in the lab's host (dev/uilab/host.lua), with the
lab's stand-in for the game's API and a fake server (dev/uilab/worlds/), and draws what it makes; the files it
read are watched, and a change runs it again, as /reload does. This server starts the host, answers its questions
(a font's widths, an item, a spell, the client's tables, an atlas) and gives the page the textures and fonts.

Where the textures come from, by the path code gives them:
  Interface\\AddOns\\SaneUI\\...      assets/optimized/Core/... (SaneUI_<Module>: assets/optimized/<Module>/...),
                                    then BUILD/, then the drafts the config names (art not chosen yet)
  Interface\\...                     Blizzard's art in references/BlizzardInterfaceArt
  a file ID                         by the listfile the config names
Settings of this computer (all optional) in ~/.config/saneui/uilab.json:
  client    a folder of the client's tables as CSV (GlobalColor, GlobalStrings, ChrClasses, ...): the game's own
            colours, strings, class and race names
  listfile  the game's file IDs to paths (CSV: id;path), for textures given by file ID
  atlas     the game's atlases (TSV: name file fileDataID width height left right top bottom tileH tileV)
  drafts    { "SaneUI/Art/Journal": "assets/generated/interface/pieces" }: addon folders served from elsewhere
  fonts     { "frizqt__.ttf": "/usr/share/fonts/...ttf" }: stand-ins for the game's own fonts, which its client
            ships compiled and cannot be read
"""
import argparse
